aimap is an IMAP4rev2 server written by Claude AI for OpenBSD in the
privilege-separated style of smtpd(8) and httpd(8). It serves the
maildirs that smtpd's maildir action writes, keeps the TLS private
key out of the process that speaks to clients, and parses mail only
in a process pledged to stdio and recvfd. It links only base system
libraries.
